CLASS:: EventSchedulerGUI
summary:: Transport and mixer window for EventScheduler
categories:: GUI
related:: Classes/EventScheduler

DESCRIPTION::
A window with Load, play/stop, record (with a Stems checkbox), a loop menu (off, infinite, 2, 4, 8 cycles) and an output menu (auto, array, fold), plus one strip per track of the loaded file (main last) with mute, solo, a dB label, a level meter, a fader on the track's router gain and the insert chain in order. Fader gains persist across plays. The window owns an link::Classes/EventScheduler:: created with code::enableMonitoring: true::.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: server
Defaults to code::Server.default::.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: loadFile
Load a Score.write file and rebuild the strips.

METHOD:: play
METHOD:: stop
METHOD:: startRecording
Transport. Recording writes code::<stem>_render.wav:: beside the loaded file (never the file's control-envelope code::.wav::).

METHOD:: scheduler
The underlying link::Classes/EventScheduler::.

METHOD:: close

EXAMPLES::
code::
s.boot;
g = EventSchedulerGUI(s);
{ g.scheduler.loadKlothoDefs }.fork;
g.loadFile("piece.json");
::
